+**IP-123.** [Stated — ⛔ **WARRANT: `File 85`, two-label class; sentence-checked**; ⏳ **OPEN EAR FLAG**] Anchor: **§14 Liturgy** ⭐⭐⭐ / §9 Eucharist — Sacrifice ⭐⭐ ; cross-ref `IP-84`, `LS-24` — ⭐⭐⭐ **THE THREE ALTAR ORIENTATIONS, AND A FIRST-PERSON VOW HE HAS ALREADY PAID FOR.** He lays out *ad orientem* (St. Francis's practice), *versus populum*, and the north end; notes the argument that St. Francis's practice is *"too sacerdotal"* and answers it from Exodus — *"the directions we get in Exodus about how the priest is supposed to face for worship is actually on the Northern Rite"* **[`s117`, speaker `A`, `[9:06]`, `@252,861–252,994`]** — so *"the actual most sacerdotal form is the one where you're on the north end."*
+
+⭐⭐⭐ **The vow, and the cost:** *"That's why I don't consider it a sin to celebrate Communion like this, but I made it a personal promise to myself But I would not ever celebrate this way."* **[`s142`, speaker `A`, `[10:59]`, `@315,663–315,911`]** His reason is representational: *"this is me presenting m it to you as if this is my meal that I'm giving to you… I want to say that I'm just the first in line, and I'm presiding over the Eucharist… I am not the one who is myself giving you the elements, which is why we're all going in the same direction."* ⭐⭐ **And he reports declining a post over it** — a parish in another diocese, a bishop who required *versus populum* for a probationary period first (*"you can do it the other way after a few months of you being there, but you've got to first do it this way"*, `s149`): *"And that wasn't the only reason I didn't, you know, take the position, but I just, I was like, that's probably not what I'm up uh for."* **[`s150`, speaker `A`, `[11:51]`, `@344,162–344,296`]**
+
+**[Analysis]** ⭐⭐ **A rare instance in the corpus of a ceremonial conviction with a stated PERSONAL COST attached rather than only a stated reason.** ⚠️⚠️ **AND THE DISTINCTION HE DRAWS IS THE ENTRY'S REAL SUBSTANCE AND MUST TRAVEL WITH ANY USE OF IT: he holds *versus populum* NOT SINFUL (*"I don't consider it a sin"*) while binding HIMSELF against it by private promise.** ⭐ **That is the same *not-sinful-but-not-for-me* shape his incense position takes from the other side — allowed for all, expected by him — and it is recorded as a structural parallel, ⛔ NOT as evidence about the incense position and NOT drafted from.** ⚠️ **He does not name the diocese, the bishop or the parish, and none is inferred.**
